# KRunner theming for new users of the desktop shell (V3 of the working brief,
# docs/SHELL_CONTRACT.md scope item 4: "KRunner: centred floating panel, material
# driven by tokens"). Installed to /etc/skel/.config/krunnerrc by the kuura-shell
# package, the same mechanism as the sibling kwinrc/kglobalshortcutsrc/kdeglobals
# skel files in this directory.
#
# WHY this one key and no others: found by booting the pinned guest image
# (krunner 6.30.0-1, plasma-workspace 6.7.5-1, kwin 6.7.5-1 - confirmed with
# `pacman -Q krunner plasma-workspace kwin plasma-desktop frameworkintegration
# kirigami-addons` in the guest) and reading KRunner's OWN KConfigXT schema,
# `/usr/share/config.kcfg/krunnersettingsbase.kcfg`. That file (`kcfgfile
# name="krunnerrc"`, group "General") declares exactly three entries -
# freeFloating (key FreeFloating, Bool, default false), historyBehavior (Enum:
# Disabled/ImmediateCompletion/CompletionSuggestion, default
# CompletionSuggestion) and retainPriorSearch (key RetainPriorSearch, Bool,
# default true) - and nothing else. Cross-checked against the compiled Behavior
# KCM (`kcm_krunnersettings.so`, scanned with `strings -a` the same way
# kwinrc's decoration/overview findings were): it exposes the standard
# KConfigXT-generated companions of exactly those three properties
# (defaultFreeFloatingValue, isFreeFloatingImmutable, freeFloatingChanged, and
# the equivalent pair for historyBehavior/retainPriorSearch) and no others -
# confirming the kcfg file is the complete, real surface, not a guess.
#
# ---- Centred FLOATING panel [General] FreeFloating ----
# freeFloating/FreeFloating is the real, verified lever - and it turned out to
# matter: KRunner's out-of-the-box default (no krunnerrc file at all, a
# genuinely fresh account) is FreeFloating=false, which docks the popup flush
# against the underside of the top panel - horizontally centred, but not
# floating. This was confirmed live: `qdbus6 org.kde.krunner /App
# org.kde.krunner.App.display` (the real D-Bus method, read from
# /usr/share/dbus-1/interfaces/org.kde.krunner.App.xml - see also
# harness/states.toml's search-open state, which opens the same window through
# the Alt+Space shortcut instead) on a fresh boot with no krunnerrc produced a
# popup touching the panel's bottom edge, screenshotted via
# harness/spike/boot_capture.sh. Writing FreeFloating=true with `kwriteconfig6
# --file krunnerrc --group General --key FreeFloating true` BEFORE that same
# trigger visibly detached the popup from the panel: same horizontal centring,
# now also vertically centred with a real gap above it - a genuine floating
# panel, not merely a cosmetic difference. FreeFloating=true is therefore set
# below as the correct, verified-real key for this requirement.
#
# ---- "Material driven by tokens" - NO REAL LEVER EXISTS, not implemented ----
# Checked independently rather than assuming the KWin decoration/Overview
# effect precedent (this file's sibling, kwinrc) carries over unchanged - it
# does not automatically, KRunner uses Plasma's frame/theme system, not
# KDecoration3 or a kwin effect config group - but the conclusion turns out to
# be the same class of finding:
#   - The kcfg schema above is exhaustive: no opacity, blur, radius or
#     "material"-shaped key exists in krunnersettingsbase.kcfg, and the KCM
#     binary's own strings confirm nothing beyond the three keys above is even
#     wired up to a settings UI.
#   - `strings -a /usr/bin/krunner` and `strings -a /usr/lib/libKF6Runner.so`,
#     grepped case-insensitively for opacity|blur|radius|corner|material|
#     background, found nothing meaningful (the krunner binary's only match was
#     an unrelated CLI help string, "Start KRunner in the background, don't
#     show it."; libKF6Runner.so had no matches at all) - KRunner's own code
#     does not parametrise any of this.
#   - The popup's frame is Plasma's generic, shared dialog background SVG
#     (/usr/share/plasma/desktoptheme/default/{opaque,translucent,solid}/
#     dialogs/background.svgz - the same asset every Plasma popup/tooltip/menu
#     uses), not something KRunner itself owns or can be pointed at a
#     per-component token from here.
#   - Whether that frame blurs its background is decided by
#     `Plasma::Theme::blurBehindEnabled()` (found by symbol name in
#     libPlasma.so.6.7.5) - a RUNTIME QUERY against the compositor's active
#     state, not a stored config value - and KWin's Blur effect is already
#     `"EnabledByDefault": true` in its own metadata
#     (/usr/share/kwin-wayland/builtin-effects/blur.json), so background blur
#     for KRunner (and every other popup) already happens out of the box,
#     globally, with nothing for this package to switch on. Its only tunable
#     ("strength"/"noise"/"saturation", found via `strings -a` on
#     kwin_blur_config.so) is a compositor-wide multiplier applied to every
#     blurred surface at once - the same class of value as kwinrc's own
#     AnimationDurationFactor finding for the Overview effect, and mapping
#     design/tokens.json's material.blur_radius (a per-surface pixel radius)
#     onto it would be exactly the kind of approximation that finding already
#     rejected. It is not done here either.
#   - Corner radius: no radius/corner key exists anywhere in the scanned
#     binaries or the kcfg; the popup's corners are whatever shape is baked
#     into the shared background.svgz asset itself - the same category of
#     finding as the Breeze window decoration's boolean-only RoundedCorners
#     lever (kwinrc, [Windeco]), except KRunner does not even have that much of
#     a toggle.
# Net result: design/tokens.json's material.bg_opacity.menu (0.7),
# material.blur_radius (36) and radius.menu (10) have NO real, KRunner-specific
# lever in this build (krunner 6.30.0-1 / plasma-workspace 6.7.5-1 / kwin
# 6.7.5-1). Per this project's own escalation rule (do not approximate a
# missing lever), this is reported rather than faked - see
# docs/SHELL_CONTRACT.md for the same finding in the document that tracks V3's
# scope.
[General]
FreeFloating=true
